# SDK configuration symbols (informational; edited via `make menuconfig`,
# stored in .config). Defaults live in .config.default.
#
# CONFIG_SDK_DISTRO          distribution codename (only "trixie" is supported:
#                            mirrors, the security include and the isolinux
#                            binaries are all trixie-specific)
# CONFIG_SDK_FLAVOUR         kernel flavour suffix, i.e. linux-image-<flavour>
#                            ("amd64" -> linux-image-amd64)
# CONFIG_SDK_INITSYSTEM      init system for the live system ("systemd")
# CONFIG_SDK_BOOTLOADER      ISO bootloader: "syslinux" (BIOS, USB+CD hybrid,
#                            recommended) or "grub2" (El Torito CD boot only -
#                            this live-build vintage cannot hybridize grub2)
# CONFIG_SDK_MEMTEST         memtest boot entry: "none" or "memtest86+"
# CONFIG_SDK_ISO_NAME        output filename (also SDK_ISO_NAME env override)
# CONFIG_SDK_ISO_VOLUME      ISO volume id, max 32 chars
# CONFIG_SDK_ISO_APPLICATION ISO application id string
# CONFIG_SDK_BOOT_TIMEOUT    seconds to wait in `make boot-test` (also
#                            SDK_BOOT_TIMEOUT env override)
# CONFIG_SDK_QEMU_MEM        VM RAM in MB for `make boot-test` (also
#                            SDK_QEMU_MEM env override)
# CONFIG_SDK_SECURITY        build chroot against security repo (NOT WORKING:
#                            this live-build writes the obsolete trixie/updates
#                            suite; security updates are shipped in the image
#                            via layers/base instead - keep unset)
# CONFIG_SDK_VOLATILE        build chroot against -updates pocket (NOT WORKING:
#                            defaults point at Ubuntu; keep unset)
#
# Package selection lives in .config.packages (NOT shell-sourced):
#   CONFIG_PACKAGE_<debian-name>=y      package will be installed
#   # CONFIG_PACKAGE_<name> is not set  explicitly deselected
# Managed via: make menuconfig (Package selection menu),
#   scripts/package list|show|add|del|check|sync|init|updatedb,
#   make package-add P=<name> (deps auto-added), make package-check.
# Locked core packages (kernel, init, iso tooling) live in
# layers/base/package-lists/core.list.chroot and cannot be deselected.
# Dependency data comes from package/db.json (scripts/package updatedb).
#
# OS-internal selection lives in .config.os-packages (NOT shell-sourced):
#   CONFIG_OS_<debian-name>=y      keep this base/live/kernel package (default)
#   # CONFIG_OS_<name> is not set  remove it at build time
# Managed via: make menuconfig (Package selection > OS internal packages),
#   scripts/package os-list|os-add|os-del|os-check|os-init,
#   make os-add P=<name>, make os-del P=<name>, make os-check.
# Removals are applied as debootstrap --exclude (LB_BOOTSTRAP_EXCLUDE,
# exported from .config.os-packages by config_trixie.sh) plus a chroot purge
# hook (config/hooks/0910-os-purge.chroot, written by `scripts/package sync`).
# Genuine OS-level additions land in
# config/package-lists/71-os-selection.list.chroot.
# Guards: live-boot, live-boot-initramfs-tools and live-config-systemd are
# boot-critical and locked; Essential=yes packages need --force.
